# secrets — phish.net API key
.env

node_modules/

# cached phish.net API responses + derived analysis (regenerate with npm run fetch && npm run analyze)
# Deliberately non-recursive: data/archive/*.json holds point-in-time model predictions
# that CANNOT be regenerated once analysis.json moves on to the next show, so they are
# committed on purpose. Do not broaden this to data/**/*.json.
data/*.json

# ...except the five files the site actually serves. Committed so a deploy is
# reproducible from the repo alone: CI has no phish.net key and should not spend minutes
# re-fetching 14MB of raw setlists on every merge. Only these small published outputs are
# tracked — the raw caches they are derived FROM stay ignored above.
!data/analysis.json
!data/songs.json
!data/venues.json
!data/songmeta.json
!data/history.json
!data/showtimes.json

# The fitted score -> probability map. Not served to anyone: analyze.js reads it and bakes
# `p` into analysis.json. Committed because it is the record of a fit that costs a 145-show
# walk-forward to reproduce, and because the raw setlists it was fitted on are ignored above
# — without this file the number could not be regenerated on a fresh clone at all.
!data/calibration.json

# Walk-forward accuracy per approach, for the Nerd Zone. Committed for the same reason as the
# calibration above: regenerating it costs a full backtest over raw setlists that are ignored,
# and analyze.js needs it to publish accuracy beside each ranking. Also not served — it is
# baked into analysis.json.
!data/arms.json

# Per-era song prevalence for the Nerd Zone what-if lenses. Same reasoning again, and one more
# besides: this one is derived from FORTY YEARS of setlists (1983-2021, ~79MB, all ignored),
# so a fresh clone could not rebuild it without re-crawling the whole phish.net archive. The
# eras have ended, so the file never legitimately changes.
!data/eras.json

# user accounts, password hashes, sessions, predictions — never publish
data/db.json

# generated deploy bundle (scripts/build-public.js) and the one-shot D1 seed
public/
data/seed.sql

# local Worker secrets + state
.dev.vars
.wrangler/
